==English==
===Verb===
{{en-verb|takes the cake|taking the cake|took the cake|taken the cake}}
#{{idiomatic|US}} To be especially [[good]] or [[outstanding]].  
#:''Thanks!  You guys '''take the cake'''.''
#:''Once the party was over, everyone agreed that Elizabeth and her Harriet Tubman getup had '''taken the cake'''.''
#{{idiomatic|US}} To be particularly [[bad]], [[objectionable]], or [[egregious]].{{jump|to be particularly bad or egregious|s}}
#:''I've seen bad grammar, but this '''takes the cake'''.''

====Synonyms====
* ''(to be good or outstanding)'': [[steal the show]]
* {{jump|s|to be particularly bad or egregious}} [[take the biscuit]]  (''British'')

